meta {
  name: Update List Products Subpath - Not Supported (Flow 5)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

patch {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/pim-product-lists/REPLACE_WITH_LIST_ID/products
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "product_ids": ["6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4"]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
  res.body.errors[0].description: contains extra_forbidden
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 -- `USER_FLOWS.md` Flow 5, against a
  throwaway list (id `6aa04ad02b6fd055ffb7cae8`, since deleted).

  ## Rules out a list-side product-assignment mechanism
  `POST /pim-product-lists/{id}/products` -- `405 Method Not Allowed`
  (route recognized at the generic subpath level, but `POST` isn't an
  accepted verb there).

  `PATCH /pim-product-lists/{id}/products` -- `422`:
  `{"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"1 validation
  error for ProductListUpdateInputDto\nproducts\n  Extra inputs are not
  permitted [type=extra_forbidden, ...]"}]}`. This reveals the generic
  subpath `PATCH` mechanism's real behavior: `{path}` is validated as a
  field name against the resource's own Update DTO
  (`ProductListUpdateInputDto` here), and the request body becomes that
  field's new value. Since `products` isn't a real field on that DTO,
  it 422s as an unrecognized extra field -- **there is no list-side way
  to manage membership at all**, confirming Flow 5's real answer: the
  only mechanism is `PATCH /products/{id}` with `static_list_ids` (see
  `02-Products-v3`), a product-side field, not anything on the list.
}
